ys in mid-September from St. Pete Polls and Change Research showed the race tied, while Republican-leaning pollsters still found Moody ahead by seven. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely or Solid R, and prediction markets give Nixon roughly a ten percent chance. The forecast expects Moody to win by around five points, with meaningful uncertainty given the mixed polling picture.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1404, "margin": -5.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2259, "margin": -4.8}]}